# Line endings are load-bearing here: the container entrypoint is `sh` and the
# Dockerfile RUN steps invoke it. A CRLF checkout (the default on Windows) makes
# the kernel look for a `sh` interpreter named `sh\r` and every boot fails with
# "no such file or directory". Upstream enforces the same rule.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
docker-compose.yml text eol=lf
.env.railway text eol=lf

*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
